  annotation "note_1771574651327_1", anchor: "extraction output has declined by an estimated thirty-one percent", text: "Thirty-one. Not thirty, not a third — thirty-one. From a site adjacent to a location that appears on no map, corrupted by a source no census acknowledges. I would dearly love to know who is conducting audits at ☽'shadow Umbrsulcavus~ and where they are filing them, because it is not with me.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771574651327_2", anchor: "dares fledglings to count past three into the fog", text: "I have already noted — on Kelm's Dark Verses — that the most accurate perimeter map of an active corruption zone exists in a children's counting game. Here is the pattern again: *count past three* is a more precise boundary marker than anything the Aurora cartographer produced with his instruments and his flag. Children's rhymes are mapping corruption geography across the Berg with better resolution than our survey infrastructure. The rhymes persist because they are sung; the surveys perish because they are filed. There is a lesson about archives in this that I am choosing to find amusing rather than devastating.", type: :commentary, display: :full
